<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-chamaeleo-calyptratus-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Holocene Chamaeleo calyptratus Turing wavelength at 260.4 µm (Pass 1) (Chamaeleo calyptratus (veiled chameleon))",
        "Holocene Chamaeleo calyptratus Turing wavelength at 260.4 µm (Pass 1) faithfully reproduces Chamaeleo calyptratus (veiled chameleon) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-chamaeleo-calyptratus-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-chamaeleo-calyptratus-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-chamaeleo-calyptratus-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-chamaeleo-calyptratus-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Chamaeleo calyptratus (veiled chameleon) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-chamaeleo-calyptratus-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Chamaeleo calyptratus (veiled chameleon)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim a calibrated micrometre measurement from the Wikimedia photograph, which has no scale bar.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim a second independent assessor.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the guanine lattice spacing is 260.4 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: A = 0.062, B = 1.150, supercritical factor 1.45, and Dv_y/Dv_x = 0.42, chosen so λ_c sits on the 260.4 µm slot scale and the pattern is a vertical bar.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: The 80 µm predecessor cutoff and the 10-wavelength (2.604 mm) successor envelope. The chronoseries has one Holocene point at 0 Ma.",
        "reported_in_source: Ligon & McGraw 2013: male Chamaeleo calyptratus change lateral stripe brightness during contests.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics du/dt = Du lap u + A - u + u^2 v, dv/dt = Dv lap v + B - u^2 v.",
        "reported_in_source: Teyssier et al. 2015: chameleon skin has a tunable guanine-nanocrystal iridophore lattice. The animals in that study are panther chameleons (Furcifer pardalis); the reported spacing is of order 100 nm.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and Murray 1981 wavenumber for a two-species reaction-diffusion system.",
        "transfer_boundary: Dermal chromatophore anatomy is transferred from the panther-chameleon study to C. calyptratus. The 260.4 µm carrier is the slot scale, not a number reported by Ligon or Teyssier." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Chamaeleo calyptratus" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Amphibia & Reptilia (Ootoka)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Chamaeleo" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-chamaeleo-calyptratus-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/chamaeleo_calyptratus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Chamaeleo calyptratus (veiled chameleon); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and Murray 1981 wavenumber for a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics du/dt = Du lap u + A - u + u^2 v, dv/dt = Dv lap v + B - u^2 v. | Ligon & McGraw 2013: male Chamaeleo calyptratus change lateral stripe brightness during contests. | Teyssier et al. 2015: chameleon skin has a tunable guanine-nanocrystal iridophore lattice. The animals in that study are panther chameleons (Furcifer pardalis); the reported spacing is of order 100 nm.; reconstructed_in_script: A = 0.062, B = 1.150, supercritical factor 1.45, and Dv_y/Dv_x = 0.42, chosen so λ_c sits on the 260.4 µm slot scale and the pattern is a vertical bar. | The 80 µm predecessor cutoff and the 10-wavelength (2.604 mm) successor envelope. The chronoseries has one Holocene point at 0 Ma.; transfer_boundary: Dermal chromatophore anatomy is transferred from the panther-chameleon study to C. calyptratus. The 260.4 µm carrier is the slot scale, not a number reported by Ligon or Teyssier.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a calibrated micrometre measurement from the Wikimedia photograph, which has no scale bar. | Does not claim the guanine lattice spacing is 260.4 µm. | Does not claim a second independent assessor.]; phenomenon_size: 241 µm (0.0002408 m, log10=-3.618 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 241 µm to 71.8 cm): 241 µm:chamaeleo-calyptratus-bioelectric-polarity, 875 µm:chamaeleo-calyptratus-vertex-packing, 1.6 cm:chamaeleo-calyptratus-turing-wavelength, 3.0 cm:chamaeleo-calyptratus-clock-wavefront, 5.0 cm:chamaeleo-calyptratus-morphogen-condensation, 6.3 cm:chamaeleo-calyptratus-flux-canalization, 7.2 cm:chamaeleo-calyptratus-elastic-buckling, 15.7 cm:chamaeleo-calyptratus-branching-tree" ;
